---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const structuredData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ItemList",
  "name": "Kawasaki H2 Engine Parts & Conversion Components",
  "description": "Specialist components for the Kawasaki supercharged H2 engine in car installations — dry sump systems, oil cooler blanking plates, wiring looms, ECU options, uprated oil pump gears, PAIR block off plates and clutch spring upgrades.",
  "url": "https://toofasttorace.com/kawasaki-h2",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Kawasaki H2 Dry Sump System",
      "url": "https://toofasttorace.com/kawasaki-h2/dry-sump-kit"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Kawasaki H2 OE Oil Cooler Blanking Plate",
      "url": "https://toofasttorace.com/kawasaki-h2/oil-cooler-blanking-plate"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Kawasaki H2 Car Conversion Wiring Loom",
      "url": "https://toofasttorace.com/kawasaki-h2/wiring-loom"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 4,
      "name": "Kawasaki H2 Standalone ECU Options",
      "url": "https://toofasttorace.com/kawasaki-h2/ecu-options"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 5,
      "name": "Kawasaki H2 High Volume Oil Pump",
      "url": "https://toofasttorace.com/kawasaki-h2/high-volume-oil-pump"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 6,
      "name": "Kawasaki H2 PAIR Block Off Plates",
      "url": "https://toofasttorace.com/kawasaki-h2/pair-block-off-plates"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 7,
      "name": "MBE 9A9 ECU with Kawasaki H2 Map",
      "url": "https://toofasttorace.com/kawasaki-h2/mbe-9a9-ecu"
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout title="Kawasaki H2 Engine Parts & Dry Sump Systems | Too Fast To Race" description="Specialist Kawasaki supercharged H2 engine parts for car installations — dry sump systems, high volume oil pumps, oil cooler blanking plates, motorsport wiring looms and standalone ECU options. Developed from real conversion experience.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(structuredData)} />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="stripe-accent"></span>
      <h1>Kawasaki H2 <span class="text-green">Engine Parts & Conversion Engineering</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">Specialist components for the supercharged H2 engine in cars — dry sump systems, oil control, looms and engine management. Developed from real conversion work, not adapted from motorcycle parts.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro + Guide Download -->
  <section class="hub-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="intro-grid">
        <div class="content-block">
          <h2>An Extraordinary Engine, <span class="text-green">With Conditions</span></h2>
          <p>The Kawasaki supercharged H2 is one of the most compelling engines available to a car builder — 998cc, forced induction from the ground up, and a power-to-weight ratio that very little else approaches at the money. It has found its way into lightweight sports cars, kit and component cars, sports racing cars, single-seaters, hillclimb specials and one-off chassis of every description.</p>
          <p>It also has requirements that the original motorcycle never had to meet. Oil control under sustained lateral loading, thermal management outside a motorcycle's airflow, and a complete replacement of the factory electrics are not optional extras — they are the difference between an engine that lasts and one that does not. Those three problems are what our H2 components exist to solve.</p>
        </div>

                <aside class="guide-aside">
          <span class="kit-card-brand">Read First</span>
          <h3>The H2 Engine Family Reference</h3>
          <p>Our full technical reference on the supercharged H2 platform — the variants and how they genuinely differ, how to identify an engine correctly, why the standard lubrication system becomes the limiting factor in a car, and what a conversion actually requires.</p>
          <a href="/kawasaki-h2/engine-specifications" class="btn btn-primary">Read the Engine Guide</a>
          <a href="/downloads/kawasaki-h2-engine-reference.pdf" class="guide-aside-pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Or download the reference (PDF) →</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

    <!-- Technical Reference -->
  <section class="reference-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="stripe-accent"></span>
        <h2>Before You <span class="text-green">Buy an Engine</span></h2>
        <p>Two things decide whether an H2 conversion works: which engine you actually have, and how it is geared once the chain drive is gone. Both are covered in full.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="reference-grid">
        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/engine-specifications" class="reference-card">
          <span class="kit-card-brand">Engine Guide</span>
          <h3>Specifications &amp; Variant Identification</h3>
          <p>The family splits into two mechanically different builds, and the ZXT00NE engine number will not tell you which one you are looking at. Compression ratios, how the variants genuinely differ, how to identify an engine correctly, and why the standard lubrication system becomes the limiting factor in a car.</p>
          <span class="kit-card-link">Read the Engine Guide →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/gear-ratios" class="reference-card">
          <span class="kit-card-brand">Gearbox Data</span>
          <h3>Gear Ratios &amp; Final Drive Selection</h3>
          <p>Verified ratios and primary reduction figures for every variant, with tooth counts. The calculation method for road speed in a direct-coupled installation, the primary reduction error that wrecks most attempts at it, and a worked example of choosing a differential.</p>
          <span class="kit-card-link">View the Ratio Data →</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="reference-proof">
        <div class="proof-figures">
          <div class="proof-figure">
            <span class="proof-number">284</span>
            <span class="proof-unit">hp</span>
            <span class="proof-label">At the crank, 13,830 rpm</span>
          </div>
          <div class="proof-figure">
            <span class="proof-number">245</span>
            <span class="proof-unit">hp</span>
            <span class="proof-label">At the wheel, 13,930 rpm</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-text">
          <p>Measured on a Dynojet 224xLC and DIN corrected — the same pull published both at the wheel and at the crank, because a crank figure on its own tells you very little without the run behind it. Torque is flat from roughly 8,000 rpm and power climbs almost linearly to nearly 14,000 without the flattening that signals a breathing or fuelling limit.</p>
          <a href="/kawasaki-h2/engine-specifications#measured-output" class="kit-card-link">See Both Dyno Plots →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Products -->
  <section class="products-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="stripe-accent"></span>
        <h2>H2 Components</h2>
        <p>Purpose-developed parts for the H2 engine in car installations. Each is explained in detail on its own page.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="parts-grid">
        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/dry-sump-kit" class="part-card part-card-feature">
          <div class="part-card-image">
            <img src="/images/kawasaki-h2/dry-sump-01.jpg" alt="Billet dry sump pan for the Kawasaki H2 engine" width="600" height="600" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <div class="part-card-body">
            <span class="kit-card-brand">Flagship Product</span>
            <h3>Dry Sump System</h3>
            <p>Three-stage scavenge dry sump for the H2 engine. Consistent oil supply regardless of cornering load or attitude, reduced windage, and the sump depth taken out of your packaging problem.</p>
            <div class="part-card-foot">
              <span class="part-card-price">Pricing to follow</span>
              <span class="kit-card-link">View Details →</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/oil-cooler-blanking-plate" class="part-card">
          <div class="part-card-body">
            <span class="kit-card-brand">Oil System</span>
            <h3>OE Oil Cooler Blanking Plate</h3>
            <p>Fitted in place of the factory oil/water heat exchanger. Oil passes out of the block and straight back in, deleting the OE cooler entirely — for installations running their own remote oil cooling. Four bolts, no plumbing.</p>
            <div class="part-card-foot">
              <span class="part-card-price">Pricing to follow</span>
              <span class="kit-card-link">View Details →</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/wiring-loom" class="part-card">
          <div class="part-card-body">
            <span class="kit-card-brand">Electrical</span>
            <h3>Car Conversion Wiring Loom</h3>
            <p>The factory loom cannot be carried into a car — immobiliser integration, ride-by-wire actuation and motorcycle connector standards all get in the way. A purpose-built loom removes that problem at the start of the project rather than after the engine is in the car.</p>
            <div class="part-card-foot">
              <span class="part-card-price">Pricing to follow</span>
              <span class="kit-card-link">View Details →</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/ecu-options" class="part-card">
          <div class="part-card-body">
            <span class="kit-card-brand">Engine Management</span>
            <h3>Standalone ECU Options</h3>
            <p>Correctly configured engine management for the H2 in car use — trigger interpretation, throttle actuation, fan and fuel pump control, warning strategy and data logging. Specified around your installation and intended use.</p>
            <div class="part-card-foot">
              <span class="part-card-price">Pricing to follow</span>
              <span class="kit-card-link">View Details →</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/high-volume-oil-pump" class="part-card">
          <div class="part-card-body">
            <span class="kit-card-brand">Oil System</span>
            <h3>High Volume Oil Pump</h3>
            <p>A wider EN26 steel gerotor raising oil pressure 30–50% across the rev range. Supplied complete with billet pump body, or as the gear set alone where a dry sump has taken over the water pump position.</p>
            <div class="part-card-foot">
              <span class="part-card-price">Pricing to follow</span>
              <span class="kit-card-link">View Details →</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/pair-block-off-plates" class="part-card">
          <div class="part-card-body">
            <span class="kit-card-brand">Induction & Emissions</span>
            <h3>PAIR Block Off Plates</h3>
            <p>Block off plates for the PAIR secondary air injection system on the Ninja H2 and Z H2. Removes redundant motorcycle emissions hardware and simplifies the engine for car installation.</p>
            <div class="part-card-foot">
              <span class="part-card-price">Pricing to follow</span>
              <span class="kit-card-link">View Details →</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a href="/kawasaki-h2/mbe-9a9-ecu" class="part-card">
          <div class="part-card-body">
            <span class="kit-card-brand">Engine Management</span>
            <h3>MBE 9A9 ECU &amp; Map</h3>
            <p>A proven motorsport ECU supplied with our own H2 base map. The hardware is available from several places — the calibration that makes a supercharged H2 run properly in a car is what you are actually buying.</p>
            <div class="part-card-foot">
              <span class="part-card-price">Pricing to follow</span>
              <span class="kit-card-link">View Details →</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="parts-note">Pricing is being finalised across the range and will be published here. In the meantime, contact us for current pricing, lead times and advice on which components your installation actually needs — we would rather specify it properly than sell you a part you do not require. Further components are in development and will be added as they are released.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Engineering Support -->
  <section class="support-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="support-grid">
        <div class="support-content">
          <h2>Conversion <span class="text-green">Engineering Support</span></h2>
          <p>Beyond the components themselves, we can support the wider engineering of an H2 installation — cooling strategy, oil system layout and tank positioning, mounting and integration, and calibration decisions appropriate to the engine specification you are working with.</p>
          <p>Our involvement in H2 engineering comes directly from encountering and solving these problems in practice rather than from reading about them. If you are early in a project, the most valuable conversation is usually the one before anything is bought.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-stats">
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-number">998</span>
            <span class="stat-unit">cc</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Supercharged Displacement</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-number">9.2</span>
            <span class="stat-unit">&times;</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Supercharger Drive Ratio to Crank Speed</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-number">3</span>
            <span class="stat-unit">Stage</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Dry Sump Scavenge System</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Related Expertise -->
  <section class="related-expertise">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="expertise-header">
        <span class="stripe-accent"></span>
        <h3>Engineering <span class="text-green">Beyond the Engine</span></h3>
        <p>An H2-powered car still needs correct suspension specification. Our chassis development expertise applies across every platform we work with.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="expertise-grid">
        <a href="/suspension" class="expertise-link">Suspension Philosophy →</a>
        <a href="/nitron-suspension" class="expertise-link">Nitron Systems →</a>
        <a href="/penske-racing-shocks" class="expertise-link">Penske Racing Shocks →</a>
        <a href="/caterham" class="expertise-link">Lightweight Chassis Development →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-content">
        <h2>Discuss Your H2 Project</h2>
        <p>Tell us about the engine, the car and how you intend to use it. We will tell you honestly what the installation needs — and what it does not.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start the Conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* Page Hero */
  .page-hero {
    padding: calc(80px + var(--space-xl)) 0 var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--tftr-darker);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.2);
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* Intro */
  .hub-intro {
    background: var(--tftr-black);
  }

  .intro-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 360px;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .content-block {
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .content-block h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .content-block p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .guide-aside {
    background: var(--tftr-dark);
    border: 1px solid rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.25);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .guide-aside h3 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--tftr-white);
    margin: 0.25rem 0 var(--space-sm);
  }

  .guide-aside p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .guide-aside .btn-primary {
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  /* Shared */
  .section-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .section-header p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .kit-card-brand {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--tftr-green);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .kit-card-link {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--tftr-white);
  }

   .guide-aside-pdf {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    transition: color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .guide-aside-pdf:hover {
    color: var(--tftr-green);
  }

  /* Technical Reference */
  .reference-section {
    background: var(--tftr-darker);
  }

  .reference-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .reference-card {
    background: var(--tftr-dark);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .reference-card:hover {
    border-color: rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.3);
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }

  .reference-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--tftr-white);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .reference-card p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    flex-grow: 1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .reference-card:hover .kit-card-link {
    color: var(--tftr-green);
  }

  .reference-proof {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  }

  .proof-figures {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .proof-figure {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--tftr-green);
    padding-left: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .proof-number {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 3rem;
    color: var(--tftr-green);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .proof-unit {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--tftr-green);
    margin-left: 0.25rem;
  }

  .proof-label {
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--tftr-grey);
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .proof-text p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .reference-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .reference-proof {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-md);
    }
  }
  
  /* Parts Grid */
  .products-section {
    background: var(--tftr-black);
  }

  .parts-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .part-card {
    background: var(--tftr-darker);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .part-card:hover {
    border-color: rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.3);
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }

  .part-card-feature {
    grid-column: span 2;
    flex-direction: row;
  }

  .part-card-image {
    background: var(--tftr-white);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex: 0 0 45%;
  }

  .part-card-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
    display: block;
  }

  .part-card-body {
    padding: var(--space-md);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .part-card-body h3 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--tftr-white);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .part-card-body p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    flex-grow: 1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .part-card-foot {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .part-card-price {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--tftr-grey);
  }

  .part-card:hover .kit-card-link {
    color: var(--tftr-green);
  }

  .parts-note {
    color: var(--tftr-grey);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    max-width: 75ch;
  }

  /* Support */
  .support-section {
    background: var(--tftr-darker);
  }

  .support-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .support-content h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .support-content p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .support-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .stat-card {
    background: var(--tftr-dark);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--tftr-green);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .stat-card .stat-number {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 3rem;
    color: var(--tftr-green);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .stat-card .stat-unit {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--tftr-green);
    margin-left: 0.25rem;
  }

  .stat-card .stat-label {
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--tftr-grey);
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }

  /* Related Expertise */
  .related-expertise {
    background: var(--tftr-black);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.2);
    padding: var(--space-lg) 0;
  }

  .expertise-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .expertise-header h3 {
